from __future__ import annotations

"""Paper-faithful B/C pre-flame ECSP model with reduced global chemistry.

The governing structure follows the high-temperature/no-convection case:
constant condensed density, Nernst--Planck species transport, local
Butler--Volmer/Faraday interfacial reaction, charge conservation and condensed
energy conservation.  The LP/PVA thermochemistry is closed by the
non-metallized global reaction and two conversion-dependent exothermic channels
reported for the 31.58/58.42/9/1 wt.% LP/H2O/PVA/H3BO3 recipe.

This module is deliberately separate from ``coupled.py``.  All v7.9.5 legacy
physics, C++ and CUDA backends remain available unchanged.  The B/C model is an
opt-in v8 backend and contains no legacy liquid-fraction, passivation,
gas-coverage, artificial temperature gate, reduced gas scalar or paper
limiting-current closure.
"""

